about anything like that, like, loves chocolate chip cookies, so that the next time I went
关于任何类似的事情，比如，喜欢巧克力豆饼干，这样下次我去

828
00:36:26.460 --> 00:36:30.820
into that casting office, I could have something that might spark a moment of connection.
那个选角办公室时，我就能有一些能激发共鸣的话题。

829
00:36:30.840 --> 00:36:31.680
Yeah, you're like, hi, Tammy.
对，你就说，嗨，塔米。

830
00:36:31.940 --> 00:36:33.660
Had any good chocolate chip cookies lately?
最近有吃到好吃的巧克力豆饼干吗？

831
00:36:33.900 --> 00:36:34.800
Pretty much.
差不多就是这样。

832
00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:35.240
Yes.
是的。

833
00:36:35.260 --> 00:36:35.960
So casual.
太随意了。

834
00:36:36.400 --> 00:36:36.880
Yeah.
是啊。

835
00:36:36.880 --> 00:36:38.740
Okay, so back to the scene.
好了，回到剧情。

836
00:36:38.880 --> 00:36:40.380
I have a little thing I spotted.
我发现了一个小细节。

837
00:36:40.700 --> 00:36:47.000
At five minutes, nine seconds, there is a poster hanging in the background of the scene.
在五分零九秒时，背景里挂着一张海报。

838
00:36:47.140 --> 00:36:49.280
It's over to the left of Michael's desk.
就在迈克尔办公桌的左边。

839
00:36:49.400 --> 00:36:50.560
It says, diversity.
上面写着，多元化。

840
00:36:51.380 --> 00:36:58.100
So that poster was made by Phil Shea using the hands of our hair and makeup crew.
那张海报是菲尔·谢伊用我们发型和化妆组工作人员的手制作的。

841
00:36:58.460 --> 00:37:01.460
Yes, that is their hands and like, I guess their arms, right?
没错，那是他们的手，还有他们的手臂，对吧？

842
00:37:01.580 --> 00:37:01.860
Yes.
是的。

843
00:37:01.980 --> 00:37:02.120
Yeah.
是啊。

844
00:37:02.460 --> 00:37:04.680
So now Pam has a talking head.
现在帕姆有一个访谈片段。

845
00:37:05.020 --> 00:37:06.580
They've done their little chant.
他们完成了他们的小口号。

846
00:37:06.880 --> 00:37:07.520
Their cheer.
他们的加油词。

847
00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:09.700
Their morning, you ugly cheer.
他们那个“早上好，你这丑八怪”的加油词。

848
00:37:09.960 --> 00:37:10.320
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

849
00:37:10.720 --> 00:37:12.720
And she just said, listen, she's here.
然后她刚说，听着，她在这儿。

850
00:37:12.880 --> 00:37:13.880
She's part of this now.
她现在也是其中的一员了。

851
00:37:14.020 --> 00:37:14.700
That's right.
没错。

852
00:37:14.880 --> 00:37:18.640
And I had a little catch at five minutes and 16 seconds.
我在5分16秒处有个小失误。

853
00:37:18.880 --> 00:37:20.280
What's up, background catch queen?
怎么了，背景失误女王？

854
00:37:20.740 --> 00:37:22.580
This is a on my face catch.
这是一个我脸上的失误。

855
00:37:22.780 --> 00:37:23.020
Oh.
哦。

856
00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:27.640
Did you notice in this episode that I have a darker pigmented lip and eye shadow?
你有没有注意到这一集里我的唇色和眼影颜色更深了？

857
00:37:28.720 --> 00:37:30.220
It's a much richer color.
颜色浓郁多了。

858
00:37:30.460 --> 00:37:31.580
No, I did not notice.
没有，我没注意到。

859
00:37:31.620 --> 00:37:32.060
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

860
00:37:32.200 --> 00:37:32.440
Okay.
好吧。

861
00:37:32.680 --> 00:37:35.160
I noticed because this was a huge thing.
我注意到了，因为这可是件大事。

862
00:37:35.400 --> 00:37:38.360
Listen, when you had dark nail polish out of nowhere, I noticed.
听着，当你突然涂了深色指甲油时，我注意到了。

863
00:37:38.540 --> 00:37:38.860
I know.
我知道。

864
00:37:39.020 --> 00:37:40.400
But your lipstick, I didn't quite notice.
但你的口红，我确实没怎么注意到。

865
00:37:40.920 --> 00:37:44.460
We usually alternated between two neutral lip shades.
我们通常在两种中性唇色之间轮换。

866
00:37:44.460 --> 00:37:51.560
But my makeup artist, Laverne, she said, I really think we could go a little bolder for Pam.
但我的化妆师拉弗恩说，我觉得我们可以给帕姆尝试更大胆一点的颜色。

867
00:37:51.720 --> 00:37:53.540
She made her first sale last week.
她上周完成了第一笔销售。

868
00:37:53.700 --> 00:37:53.920
Yeah.
是啊。

869
00:37:53.920 --> 00:37:55.120
She's got her blazer.
她穿上了她的西装外套。

870
00:37:55.380 --> 00:37:55.840
Yeah.
是啊。

871
00:37:56.020 --> 00:37:56.260
Yeah.
是啊。

872
00:37:56.260 --> 00:38:00.460
So how can we continue to tell the story of her growing confidence?
那么我们该如何继续讲述她自信心增长的故事呢？

873
00:38:00.920 --> 00:38:02.520
So we went with a bolder lip.
所以我们选择了更大胆的唇色。

874
00:38:03.080 --> 00:38:04.080
I like it.
我喜欢。

875
00:38:04.200 --> 00:38:04.580
Thank you.
谢谢。

876
00:38:05.120 --> 00:38:07.180
Our next scene is Charles and Dwight.
下一场戏是查尔斯和德怀特的。

877
00:38:07.320 --> 00:38:08.860
They're in Charles's office.
他们在查尔斯的办公室里。

878
00:38:09.280 --> 00:38:11.400
Note his shoulders, please.
请注意他的肩膀。

879
00:38:11.960 --> 00:38:12.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

880
00:38:12.700 --> 00:38:17.180
Also, please note that Rain's entire watch is exposed because his sleeves are too short.
另外，请注意雷恩的整块手表都露出来了，因为他的袖子太短了。

881
00:38:17.280 --> 00:38:17.420
Okay.
好的。

882
00:38:17.600 --> 00:38:18.640
Five minutes, 39 seconds.
5分39秒。

883
00:38:18.820 --> 00:38:19.020
All right.
好的。

884
00:38:19.320 --> 00:38:23.720
So basically, Charles wants to know if Dwight is happy at the company, you know?
基本上，查尔斯想知道德怀特在公司过得开不开心，你懂的。

885
00:38:23.860 --> 00:38:25.820
And he invites him out to drinks.
于是他邀请他去喝一杯。

886
00:38:26.260 --> 00:38:26.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

887
00:38:26.880 --> 00:38:31.260
So in the background of this scene, you can see Jim, Jenna.
在这场戏的背景里，你可以看到吉姆和珍娜。

888
00:38:32.060 --> 00:38:38.020
John has angled his computer because he's clearly like surfing the internet or checking email or something.
约翰把电脑的角度调了一下，因为他显然是在上网或者查邮件之类的。

889
00:38:38.340 --> 00:38:43.560
So while I was watching this scene, the first time I just watched it just to watch it, then I was like, wait a second.
所以当我第一次看这场戏时，我只是随便看看，然后我心想，等一下。

890
00:38:44.020 --> 00:38:46.780
John's doing email in the background and the way back.
约翰在背景深处处理邮件呢。

891
00:38:47.100 --> 00:38:52.360
This scene also has a line I love when Charles says to Dwight, you're so focused.
这场戏里还有一句我特别喜欢的台词，查尔斯对德怀特说：你真专注。

892
00:38:52.520 --> 00:38:53.600
And Dwight says, like a wolf.
德怀特回答说：像狼一样。

893
00:38:53.760 --> 00:38:54.060
Thank you.
谢谢。

894
00:38:56.840 --> 00:39:02.540
Well, Rain was asked in an interview what he thought drinks between Dwight and Charles might entail.
嗯，雷恩在一次采访中被问到，他认为德怀特和查尔斯一起喝酒会是什么样。

895
00:39:02.740 --> 00:39:03.020
Yeah.
是啊。

896
00:39:03.420 --> 00:39:04.440
And this was his answer.
这是他的回答。

897
00:39:04.700 --> 00:39:10.780
He said, probably Charles getting really bored after about eight minutes and making up an excuse to leave.
他说，大概是查尔斯在八分钟后感到非常无聊，然后找借口离开。

898
00:39:11.160 --> 00:39:17.160
He was also asked about his decision to choose Dunder Mifflin over Michael Scott Paper Company.
他还被问到了选择邓德·米夫林而不是迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司的决定。

899
00:39:17.160 --> 00:39:18.340
What did he say?
他怎么说？

900
00:39:18.560 --> 00:39:22.760
He said, Dwight is loyal to whoever values loyalty the moSt.
他说，德怀特忠诚于任何最看重忠诚的人。

901
00:39:22.800 --> 00:39:27.160
And in this case, Dunder Mifflin honors loyalty with an actual paycheck.
在这种情况下，邓德·米夫林公司用实实在在的薪水来回报忠诚。

902
00:39:27.500 --> 00:39:30.620
And that is why he chose Dunder Mifflin.
这就是他选择邓德·米夫林的原因。

903
00:39:30.620 --> 00:39:38.160
I also want to point out in this scene that Charles is still drinking out of his Sadekoy steel insulated coffee mug.
我还想指出，在这一幕里，查尔斯依然在用他那个萨德科伊（Sadekoy）牌钢制保温咖啡杯喝水。

904
00:39:38.300 --> 00:39:40.160
And I have to say, I think it's a betrayal.
我不得不说，我觉得这是一种背叛。

905
00:39:40.500 --> 00:39:42.540
You're out of the steel business, Charles.
你已经不是钢材行业的人了，查尔斯。

906
00:39:42.840 --> 00:39:43.820
Let it go.
算了吧。

907
00:39:44.200 --> 00:39:46.740
Get a Dunder Mifflin insulated mug already.
赶紧换个邓德·米夫林的保温杯吧。

908
00:39:46.920 --> 00:39:47.240
Yeah.
没错。

909
00:39:47.500 --> 00:39:50.300
What is your attachment to your Sadekoy steel mug?
你对那个萨德科伊钢制杯子到底有什么执念？

910
00:39:50.300 --> 00:39:53.040
You know corporate gave him a mug, but he's not using it.
你知道公司给了他一个杯子，但他没在用。

911
00:39:53.100 --> 00:39:53.600
Why not?
为什么不用？

912
00:39:53.920 --> 00:39:53.970
That's a choice.
这是一种选择。

913
00:39:54.160 --> 00:39:55.160
That's what I'm saying.
我就是这个意思。

914
00:39:55.460 --> 00:39:55.600
Yeah.
是啊。

915
00:39:55.960 --> 00:39:57.100
I think Michael knows.
我觉得迈克尔知道。

916
00:39:57.280 --> 00:39:59.140
This guy, he's a steel man at heart.
这家伙，他骨子里就是个搞钢材的。

917
00:39:59.380 --> 00:39:59.640
Right.
对。

918
00:40:00.180 --> 00:40:02.340
This next scene is amazing.
接下来这一幕太棒了。

919
00:40:02.660 --> 00:40:02.960
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

920
00:40:03.680 --> 00:40:09.320
Michael calls Dwight to ask about Dunder Mifflin's pricing for Ed's tires.
迈克尔打电话给德怀特，询问邓德·米夫林给埃德轮胎的报价。

921
00:40:09.740 --> 00:40:09.840
Yeah.
嗯。

922
00:40:09.840 --> 00:40:11.060
He wants to undercut them.
他想压低价格。

923
00:40:11.240 --> 00:40:11.460
Right.
没错。

924
00:40:11.800 --> 00:40:14.280
And this is when Dwight's internal conflict begins.
这就是德怀特内心冲突开始的时候。

925
00:40:14.480 --> 00:40:15.500
Yeah, he starts to waffle.
是啊，他开始动摇了。

926
00:40:15.780 --> 00:40:17.920
Well, because Charles has invited him to drinks.
嗯，因为查尔斯邀请他去喝酒了。

927
00:40:18.080 --> 00:40:18.340
I know.
我知道。

928
00:40:18.340 --> 00:40:19.680
Michael never invited him to drinks.
迈克尔从来没邀请过他去喝酒。

929
00:40:19.700 --> 00:40:20.120
I know.
我知道。

930
00:40:20.300 --> 00:40:22.820
So he tells Michael something's come up.
所以他告诉迈克尔说有事走不开。

931
00:40:22.940 --> 00:40:23.240
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

932
00:40:23.920 --> 00:40:26.440
And Michael's like, oh my gosh, is it Moe's?
迈克尔就说，天哪，是莫斯（Moe's）出事了吗？

933
00:40:26.540 --> 00:40:27.700
Did you cover up the well?
你把那口井盖上了吗？

934
00:40:28.540 --> 00:40:30.020
What is that backstory?
那背后的故事是什么？

935
00:40:30.280 --> 00:40:31.080
I don't know.
我不知道。

936
00:40:31.200 --> 00:40:32.840
Has Moe's fallen in the well numerous times?
莫斯是不是掉进井里好多次了？

937
00:40:32.840 --> 00:40:33.640
Of course he has.
当然掉进去过。

938
00:40:34.200 --> 00:40:38.340
He's probably fallen and been gone for like two days, and then they find him in the well.
他可能掉进去失踪了两天，然后他们才在井里发现他。

939
00:40:38.500 --> 00:40:39.960
I love comedy like that.
我喜欢这种喜剧桥段。

940
00:40:40.240 --> 00:40:42.080
It's there, and then it goes away.
它就在那儿，然后又消失了。

941
00:40:42.340 --> 00:40:43.320
Yeah, you just throw it away.
是啊，随手就抛出来了。

942
00:40:43.880 --> 00:40:45.000
Michael's not getting it.
迈克尔没听懂。

943
00:40:45.100 --> 00:40:45.820
He's not.
他没听懂。

944
00:40:46.080 --> 00:40:48.080
Dwight starts kind of talking in code.
德怀特开始用暗语说话了。

945
00:40:48.080 --> 00:40:50.800
He's kind of like, things are changing faSt.
他大概是想说，情况变化得很快。

946
00:40:51.020 --> 00:40:51.900
And, you know.
而且，你知道的。

947
00:40:52.000 --> 00:40:53.180
There's a cool new guy.
有个很酷的新人来了。

948
00:40:53.480 --> 00:40:57.040
And I don't think he'd like it if I helped even my personal hero.
我觉得如果我帮了我的个人英雄，他肯定会不高兴的。

949
00:40:57.680 --> 00:40:59.700
And Michael's like, what are you talking about?
迈克尔就问，你在说什么呢？

950
00:40:59.900 --> 00:41:00.880
What are you talking about?
你到底在说什么？

951
00:41:00.880 --> 00:41:07.580
So Pam and Ryan are like, have to write on a notepad to help Michael understand what Dwight is saying.
帕姆和瑞安不得不写在记事本上，来帮迈克尔理解德怀特在说什么。

952
00:41:07.820 --> 00:41:11.040
And then Steve is Michael, reads the notepad.
然后史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔读了记事本。

953
00:41:11.360 --> 00:41:18.640
All the expressions that come over Steve's face, as Michael figures this out, I was blown away.
当史蒂夫弄明白这一切时，他脸上浮现出的所有表情，简直让我惊叹不已。

954
00:41:18.860 --> 00:41:22.860
I said, give Steve all of the awards, and that's why I drew a trophy.
我说，把所有的奖项都颁给史蒂夫吧，这就是我画了一个奖杯的原因。

955
00:41:24.840 --> 00:41:27.720
Seriously, though, this is an amazing performance.
说真的，这表演太棒了。

956
00:41:28.080 --> 00:41:29.900
It's so subtle and nuanced.
非常细腻，层次丰富。

957
00:41:30.100 --> 00:41:39.580
And Steve, I loved every single thing you did as Michael being clueless, and then not believing the note they're holding up, but then figuring it out, and then being like,
史蒂夫，我喜欢你作为迈克尔所做的一切，从一头雾水，到不相信他们举着的纸条，再到恍然大悟，然后表现出，

958
00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:40.100
oh my God.
天哪。

959
00:41:40.240 --> 00:41:41.120
And then being betrayed.
然后感到被背叛。

960
00:41:41.540 --> 00:41:42.320
Like, all of it.
真的，所有这些情绪。

961
00:41:42.320 --> 00:41:46.920
It is really hard to play realization as an actor.
作为演员，要演出那种“恍然大悟”的感觉真的很难。

962
00:41:47.100 --> 00:41:47.300
Yeah.
没错。

963
00:41:47.500 --> 00:41:49.240
Because you know the information.
因为你已经知道剧情信息了。

964
00:41:49.240 --> 00:41:50.760
You had to memorize it.
你必须背下来。

965
00:41:50.860 --> 00:41:51.920
You had to read the script.
你必须读过剧本。

966
00:41:51.920 --> 00:41:53.360
You know where the scene is going.
你知道这场戏的走向。

967
00:41:53.620 --> 00:41:53.980
Yes.
是的。

968
00:41:54.200 --> 00:41:59.560
And so to play all of that, it is like one of the hardest things to do as an actor.
所以要演出那种过程，是演员最难做到的事情之一。

969
00:41:59.800 --> 00:42:02.040
And then to do it comedically, amazing.
而且还要用喜剧的方式表现出来，太厉害了。

970
00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:07.400
We got a fan question about this scene from Kelton O, who said,
我们收到一个关于这场戏的粉丝提问，来自Kelton O，他问，

971
00:42:07.400 --> 00:42:12.500
how is it that Pam and Ryan can hear both sides of this phone call?
为什么帕姆和瑞安能听到这通电话的两头？

972
00:42:13.200 --> 00:42:13.560
Yeah.
是啊。

973
00:42:13.940 --> 00:42:16.960
They seem to hear Dwight so clearly through the phone.
他们似乎能通过电话清楚地听到德怀特的声音。

974
00:42:17.500 --> 00:42:23.720
Well, this is very funny, Kelton, because Rain was actually right off camera.
嗯，这很有趣，Kelton，因为雷恩当时其实就在镜头外。

975
00:42:24.060 --> 00:42:24.580
Yeah.
没错。

976
00:42:24.740 --> 00:42:26.340
Doing his side of the phone call.
在演他那边的通话内容。

977
00:42:26.460 --> 00:42:28.160
We could totally hear him.
我们完全能听到他的声音。

978
00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:30.340
Rain actually had to come into work that day.
雷恩那天其实不得不来上班。

979
00:42:30.480 --> 00:42:32.120
He did not have anything else to shoot.
他没有其他戏份要拍。

980
00:42:32.360 --> 00:42:36.140
All he did was stand off camera and read his side of the phone call.
他所做的就是站在镜头外，读他那边的通话台词。

981
00:42:36.140 --> 00:42:37.940
Well, it's actually a thing.
嗯，这其实是一种惯例。

982
00:42:38.100 --> 00:42:39.960
It's called doing off camera work.
这叫“画外音工作”。

983
00:42:40.320 --> 00:42:43.320
And that is often how different sides of a phone call are done.
电话两头的戏通常就是这样拍的。

984
00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:49.400
We did not have the capability to like call into that office.
我们没有那种能力直接打进那个办公室。

985
00:42:49.620 --> 00:42:50.000
Right.
对。

986
00:42:50.340 --> 00:42:51.460
Like we did upstairs.
就像我们在楼上那样。

987
00:42:51.940 --> 00:42:53.800
Because it was a closet and a fakie phone.
因为那只是个储藏室，电话也是假的。

988
00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:54.380
Yes.
没错。

989
00:42:54.660 --> 00:42:57.860
I thought I could see how they were cheating it a little because
我觉得我能看出他们是怎么稍微作弊的，因为

990
00:42:57.860 --> 00:43:00.040
Michael is kind of holding the phone out.
迈克尔把电话拿得有点远。

991
00:43:00.240 --> 00:43:03.000
So you would assume if he had the volume pretty high up,
所以你会假设如果他把音量调得很高，

992
00:43:03.100 --> 00:43:05.220
it's a tiny room that you guys could probably hear.
那是个很小的房间，你们大概能听到。

993
00:43:05.220 --> 00:43:08.200
We also had a fan catch from Maya R.
我们还收到了Maya R.的一个粉丝发现。

994
00:43:08.560 --> 00:43:10.080
Who said this, Angela?
安吉拉，她说了这个，

995
00:43:10.380 --> 00:43:10.720
What?
什么？

996
00:43:11.180 --> 00:43:12.900
This went right to my heart.
这直接触动了我的心。

997
00:43:13.160 --> 00:43:13.960
She said,
她说，

998
00:43:14.180 --> 00:43:17.320
I noticed a paper pro stapler on Pam and Ryan's table.
我注意到帕姆和瑞安的桌子上有一个Paper Pro订书机。

999
00:43:17.500 --> 00:43:21.960
And my mom actually works for the company that sells these staplers.
我妈妈正好就在销售这些订书机的公司工作。

1000
00:43:22.240 --> 00:43:27.440
It originated in Pennsylvania before merging with Boss Stitch.
它最初起源于宾夕法尼亚州，后来与Boss Stitch合并了。

1001
00:43:27.720 --> 00:43:30.880
Could this be why the stapler was used in this episode?
这难道就是这一集里用到订书机的原因吗？

1002
00:43:32.000 --> 00:43:36.260
I don't know, Maya, but I brought my paper pro stapler today.
我不知道，玛雅，但我今天带了我的Paper Pro订书机来了。

1003
00:43:36.600 --> 00:43:36.740
You did?
你带了？

1004
00:43:36.760 --> 00:43:37.960
I got to try it out.
我得试用一下。

1005
00:43:38.180 --> 00:43:38.580
All right.
好吧。

1006
00:43:39.560 --> 00:43:40.720
I brought champagne.
我带了香槟。

1007
00:43:40.900 --> 00:43:41.820
Jenna brought a stapler.
珍娜带了个订书机。

1008
00:43:42.040 --> 00:43:42.720
Here it is.
在这儿呢。

1009
00:43:43.700 --> 00:43:44.500
Now watch.
看好了。

1010
00:43:45.420 --> 00:43:46.740
Do I get to do it?
我可以试一下吗？

1011
00:43:46.860 --> 00:43:47.180
Yes.
可以。

1012
00:43:47.780 --> 00:43:49.740
I am going to do it with a single finger.
我打算只用一根手指来操作。

1013
00:43:49.820 --> 00:43:50.180
Wait, wait.
等等，等等。

1014
00:43:50.340 --> 00:43:50.480
Here.
给你。

1015
00:43:50.600 --> 00:43:52.860
Now, I wish I'd brought a regular stapler.
现在我倒希望我带的是个普通订书机。

1016
00:43:53.000 --> 00:43:54.540
I had meant to bring a regular stapler.
我本来是打算带个普通订书机的。

1017
00:43:54.540 --> 00:43:55.640
I'm sure there is one.
我相信肯定有一个。

1018
00:43:55.800 --> 00:43:56.160
Okay, ready?
好了，准备好了吗？

1019
00:43:56.160 --> 00:43:56.540
Watch this.
看这个。

1020
00:43:59.190 --> 00:44:01.010
Can you hear the clicking mechanism?
你能听到那个咔哒声吗？

1021
00:44:01.190 --> 00:44:02.150
Listen to the air pressure.
听听这气压的声音。

1022
00:44:03.970 --> 00:44:04.950
I heard that.
我听到了。

1023
00:44:05.530 --> 00:44:06.870
It is amazing.
太神奇了。

1024
00:44:07.130 --> 00:44:07.750
Try it.
你试试。

1025
00:44:07.930 --> 00:44:08.730
Okay, I'm going to try it.
好，我来试试。

1026
00:44:08.790 --> 00:44:09.630
Staple something.
订点什么东西。

1027
00:44:09.850 --> 00:44:10.750
I'm going to staple something.
我要订点什么东西。

1028
00:44:10.750 --> 00:44:13.570
It's not a regular stapler where you get a kajunk.
它不像普通订书机那样会发出“咔哒”一声。

1029
00:44:14.330 --> 00:44:15.650
It's like kch.
它听起来像“嘶”的一声。

1030
00:44:16.610 --> 00:44:17.930
Okay, that's very hard.
好吧，这真的很难。

1031
00:44:17.930 --> 00:44:19.270
You can do it with one finger.
你可以只用一根手指操作的。

1032
00:44:19.490 --> 00:44:20.110
Okay, ready?
好了，准备好了吗？

1033
00:44:20.310 --> 00:44:20.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1034
00:44:21.850 --> 00:44:22.850
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

1035
00:44:23.070 --> 00:44:24.570
I see what you're talking about.
我明白你在说什么了。

1036
00:44:24.710 --> 00:44:26.230
There's like a spring or something.
里面好像有个弹簧之类的东西。

1037
00:44:27.430 --> 00:44:28.030
I see.
我明白了。

1038
00:44:28.230 --> 00:44:28.910
Shut up.
闭嘴。

1039
00:44:29.190 --> 00:44:31.030
I bought you a Paper Pro stapler.
我给你买了个Paper Pro订书机。

1040
00:44:31.170 --> 00:44:31.310
Yay!
耶！

1041
00:44:31.310 --> 00:44:32.970
Sam, I have one for you.
萨姆，我也有一个给你。

1042
00:44:33.230 --> 00:44:33.430
Woo-hoo!
呜呼！

1043
00:44:33.430 --> 00:44:33.930
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1044
00:44:34.290 --> 00:44:35.750
Cassie, I have one for you.
凯西，我也有一个给你。

1045
00:44:36.290 --> 00:44:37.110
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1046
00:44:37.350 --> 00:44:37.970
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1047
00:44:38.270 --> 00:44:39.370
You need to have it.
你得拥有一个。

1048
00:44:40.170 --> 00:44:42.790
Here's the last thing I'll say about the stapler, I think.
关于订书机，我想这是我要说的最后一件事了。

1049
00:44:43.730 --> 00:44:45.630
I don't think you're done talking about it.
我觉得你还没说完呢。

1050
00:44:45.850 --> 00:44:47.010
Don't make that promise.
别轻易许下这种承诺。

1051
00:44:48.650 --> 00:44:54.590
Sometimes when we do these acting jobs, you acquire a new skill, maybe, that you didn't have before.
有时候我们做这些表演工作时，可能会掌握一项以前从未有过的新技能。

1052
00:44:54.590 --> 00:44:58.730
When I did Blades of Glory, I had to train with a ice skating coach.
拍《冰刀双人组》的时候，我得跟着一位滑冰教练训练。

1053
00:44:58.910 --> 00:45:01.270
I learned how to be quite a good ice skater.
我学会了怎么滑冰，而且滑得还不错。

1054
00:45:01.510 --> 00:45:01.670
Sure.
当然。

1055
00:45:02.330 --> 00:45:06.450
When I did Walk Hard, I took a little bit of horse riding lessons.
拍《摇滚之王》的时候，我上过一点骑马课。

1056
00:45:06.830 --> 00:45:08.250
It's like a fun perk.
这就像是一种有趣的额外福利。

1057
00:45:08.450 --> 00:45:09.490
You get these skills.
你能获得这些技能。

1058
00:45:09.850 --> 00:45:09.990
Right.
没错。

1059
00:45:10.350 --> 00:45:12.750
Sometimes you get introduced to an item.
有时候你会接触到某种物品。

1060
00:45:13.250 --> 00:45:20.090
I remember when I did Splitting Up Together, there was just this amazing set of pajamas that I'd never heard of before.
我记得拍《离婚再一起》的时候，有一套很棒的睡衣，我以前从没听说过。

1061
00:45:20.390 --> 00:45:22.750
And after wearing them on the show, I bought three pairs.
在节目里穿过之后，我买了三套。

1062
00:45:22.750 --> 00:45:25.690
I am now a lifelong fan of Sass shoes.
我现在是Sass品牌睡衣的终身粉丝了。

1063
00:45:26.430 --> 00:45:26.930
Exactly.
确实。

1064
00:45:27.230 --> 00:45:30.050
That is what this Paper Pro stapler was for me.
这款Paper Pro订书机对我来说就是这样。

1065
00:45:30.150 --> 00:45:32.970
And it was all thanks to Michael Scott Paper Company.
这一切都要归功于迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1066
00:45:33.150 --> 00:45:33.810
Well, there you go.
好吧，原来是这样。

1067
00:45:34.510 --> 00:45:38.810
Before we go to break, I have one more thing to point out about this scene.
在进入休息时间之前，关于这一幕我还有一点要指出。

1068
00:45:38.990 --> 00:45:40.950
It's at 6 minutes, 11 seconds.
在6分11秒的时候。

1069
00:45:41.170 --> 00:45:44.070
It is a very good shot of our second goldfish.
那是我们第二条金鱼的一个非常清晰的镜头。

1070
00:45:44.470 --> 00:45:45.070
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1071
00:45:45.330 --> 00:45:46.970
Our first goldfish was orange.
我们的第一条金鱼是橙色的。

1072
00:45:46.970 --> 00:45:48.250
That goldfish is gone.
那条金鱼已经不在了。

1073
00:45:48.250 --> 00:45:52.750
This week, it is a red, orange, white, and black spotted fish.
这周换成了一条红、橙、白、黑相间的花斑鱼。

1074
00:45:53.290 --> 00:45:56.730
And we got a letter from Jess L., who said,
我们收到了一封来自Jess L.的信，她说：

1075
00:45:56.950 --> 00:46:00.850
I spent 10 years working in pet stores as an aquatic specialist,
我曾在宠物店做了10年的水族专家，

1076
00:46:00.850 --> 00:46:07.670
and pet industry employees have been wondering for years whether or not the changing of the goldfish were a planned bit.
宠物行业的员工多年来一直想知道，频繁更换金鱼是不是一个预先设计好的梗。

1077
00:46:07.870 --> 00:46:10.190
Now, we said last week it was.
我们上周说过，确实是。

1078
00:46:10.190 --> 00:46:16.270
But she goes on to say, anyone who works in fish departments knows goldfish deaths are common.
但她接着说，任何在水族部门工作的人都知道，金鱼死亡是很常见的。

1079
00:46:16.430 --> 00:46:23.490
And a lot of us in the industry assume that the props people chose to make a bit out of the situation.
我们业内很多人都认为，是道具组决定利用这种情况来制造一个梗。

1080
00:46:24.250 --> 00:46:29.930
And just so you know, goldfish should have about 10 gallons of water per fish,
顺便告诉大家，每条金鱼应该有大约10加仑的水，

1081
00:46:29.950 --> 00:46:33.250
and it requires filtration to truly thrive in captivity.
而且需要过滤系统才能在人工饲养环境下真正茁壮成长。

1082
00:46:33.810 --> 00:46:39.750
She, I think, wanted us to know that because any of you out there with goldfish trying to keep them alive,
我想她是想让我们知道这一点，因为你们当中任何养金鱼并试图让它们活下去的人，

1083
00:46:39.750 --> 00:46:40.710
that could really help.
这真的会有所帮助。

1084
00:46:40.890 --> 00:46:42.650
I think that's solid advice.
我觉得这是很中肯的建议。

1085
00:46:43.190 --> 00:46:43.690
All right.
好的。

1086
00:46:43.770 --> 00:46:44.430
That's all I got.
我要说的就这些。

1087
00:46:44.690 --> 00:46:50.110
Well, I have something delicious coming up with Jim and Andy that I can't wait to share.
我这儿有一段吉姆和安迪的精彩片段，迫不及待想和大家分享。

1088
00:46:50.410 --> 00:46:50.690
Ooh.
哦。

1089
00:46:50.890 --> 00:46:53.010
It just brought me so much joy.
它真的带给我太多快乐了。

1090
00:46:53.750 --> 00:46:56.130
And why don't we take a break, and I'll come back with that.
我们先休息一下，回来后再分享。

1091
00:46:56.230 --> 00:46:56.850
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1092
00:46:57.050 --> 00:47:07.740
We are back.
我们回来了。

1093
00:47:07.960 --> 00:47:10.600
I love this Jim and Andy scene.
我喜欢这一幕吉姆和安迪的戏。

1094
00:47:10.600 --> 00:47:16.280
Jim is going to approach Andy, and he's going to say, hey, Andy, you know what?
吉姆走近安迪，他说，嘿，安迪，你知道吗？

1095
00:47:16.340 --> 00:47:17.600
I've been thinking about what you said.
我一直在想你说的话。

1096
00:47:17.900 --> 00:47:19.060
Andy's like, noish.
安迪说，不错嘛。

1097
00:47:20.060 --> 00:47:22.600
And Jim's like, I just don't know if I can do it.
吉姆说，我只是不知道我能不能做到。

1098
00:47:23.080 --> 00:47:27.560
Andy's like, that's interesting because I hear what you're saying is that you want to do it,
安迪说，这很有趣，因为我听出你的意思是你想做，

1099
00:47:27.660 --> 00:47:28.780
which means you can do it.
这意味着你一定能做到。

1100
00:47:28.920 --> 00:47:32.580
Believe me, I broke up with Angela, and I'm like the happiest guy ever.
相信我，我和安吉拉分手了，我现在可是世界上最快乐的人。

1101
00:47:32.880 --> 00:47:34.180
I mean, I am so happy.
我是说，我真的太开心了。

1102
00:47:34.320 --> 00:47:35.560
I am so happy.
我真的太开心了。

1103
00:47:35.800 --> 00:47:37.520
Like total freedom, you know?
就像彻底自由了一样，你懂吗？

1104
00:47:37.520 --> 00:47:40.840
Well, and Jim says, it's just that Pam gets me through the day.
嗯，吉姆说，帕姆是他支撑过每一天的动力。

1105
00:47:41.140 --> 00:47:42.600
Like I really rely on her.
就像我真的很依赖她一样。

1106
00:47:42.740 --> 00:47:44.440
I'm pretty emotionally needy.
我在情感上挺粘人的。

1107
00:47:45.260 --> 00:47:47.060
And Andy says, and you know what?
安迪说，你知道吗？

1108
00:47:47.060 --> 00:47:47.820
I'm here for you.
我会一直陪着你。

1109
00:47:48.060 --> 00:47:50.060
Let me be your traveling pants.
让我做你的“牛仔裤”吧。

1110
00:47:50.800 --> 00:47:52.080
That was all scripted.
那全是照着剧本演的。

1111
00:47:52.520 --> 00:47:55.940
And in the script, it says that Jim and Andy do a little knuckles bump.
剧本里写着吉姆和安迪要碰一下拳头。

1112
00:47:56.140 --> 00:47:56.400
Yeah.
没错。

1113
00:47:56.580 --> 00:47:58.840
And they just simply say knuckles.
他们就简单地说声“碰拳”。

1114
00:47:59.100 --> 00:48:00.520
And that's the end of the scene.
然后那一幕就结束了。

1115
00:48:00.680 --> 00:48:00.920
Okay.
好的。

1116
00:48:00.920 --> 00:48:06.620
Well, in our version, Jim goes to give the knuckles, and Andy leans in and puts his cheek
但在我们的版本里，吉姆去碰拳时，安迪凑了过来，把脸

1117
00:48:06.620 --> 00:48:07.720
in front of the knuckles.
凑到了拳头前面。

1118
00:48:08.340 --> 00:48:10.380
And Jim just starts to laugh.
吉姆就开始笑了。

1119
00:48:10.600 --> 00:48:13.720
And he's like, dude, you know I meant knuckles.
他说，老兄，你知道我是要碰拳吧。

1120
00:48:13.860 --> 00:48:14.820
And he's like, yeah, knuckles.
安迪回道，是啊，碰拳。

1121
00:48:15.500 --> 00:48:15.880
All right.
好吧。

1122
00:48:16.040 --> 00:48:17.760
So Ed just improvised that.
所以那是艾德即兴发挥的。

1123
00:48:17.900 --> 00:48:19.000
That whole moment.
整个那一刻。

1124
00:48:19.260 --> 00:48:21.500
Go to 8 minutes, 26 seconds.
跳到8分26秒处。

1125
00:48:21.820 --> 00:48:27.020
John is laughing at Ed because he didn't know Ed was going to lean his face into the knuckle
约翰在笑艾德，因为他不知道艾德会把脸凑到碰拳的

1126
00:48:27.020 --> 00:48:27.380
bump.
位置上。

1127
00:48:27.840 --> 00:48:29.160
And it made it in.
而这一幕被保留了下来。

1128
00:48:29.300 --> 00:48:32.160
And it just brought me joy because I just see these two guys.
这让我感到很开心，因为我看到了这两个人。

1129
00:48:32.160 --> 00:48:35.400
And I see their friendship at 8 minutes, 26 seconds.
在8分26秒，我看到了他们的友谊。

1130
00:48:35.840 --> 00:48:40.860
Well, when Andy said, I'll be your traveling pants, that made me think of our director,
当安迪说“我会做你的牛仔裤”时，让我想起了我们的导演，

1131
00:48:40.940 --> 00:48:44.420
Ken Kwapis, who directed The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants.
肯·卡皮斯，他执导了《牛仔裤的夏天》。

1132
00:48:44.420 --> 00:48:44.800
Yes.
没错。

1133
00:48:44.900 --> 00:48:47.060
And you and I went together to go see it.
我们俩还一起去看了那部电影。

1134
00:48:47.200 --> 00:48:51.800
I remember watching that movie because there was this really handsome.
我记得看那部电影是因为里面有个特别帅的男人。

1135
00:48:52.480 --> 00:48:53.920
It made us want to go to Greece.
那部电影让我们想去希腊。

1136
00:48:54.120 --> 00:48:56.420
Remember after that movie, we're like, we should go to Greece.
还记得看完电影后，我们说，我们应该去希腊。

1137
00:48:56.660 --> 00:48:57.280
We really should.
我们真的应该去。

1138
00:48:57.380 --> 00:48:58.420
We should still go to Greece.
我们还是应该去希腊。

1139
00:48:58.440 --> 00:48:58.860
We should.
我们应该去。

1140
00:48:59.300 --> 00:49:02.060
Well, now we have another scene out by the dumpster.
好了，现在我们还有一场在垃圾桶旁边的戏。

1141
00:49:02.940 --> 00:49:05.020
Michael is going to meet Dwight again.
迈克尔又要去见德怀特了。

1142
00:49:05.020 --> 00:49:05.820
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1143
00:49:06.480 --> 00:49:07.420
It's a setup.
这是个圈套。

1144
00:49:08.100 --> 00:49:08.380
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1145
00:49:08.700 --> 00:49:09.620
Charles is there.
查尔斯也在那儿。

1146
00:49:10.280 --> 00:49:15.700
And Charles is going to tell Michael to leave Dunder Mifflin alone and to stop pestering Dwight
查尔斯要告诉迈克尔离邓德·米夫林远点，别再缠着德怀特

1147
00:49:15.700 --> 00:49:16.460
for info.
打听消息了。

1148
00:49:16.820 --> 00:49:19.000
I have two things to point out about this scene.
关于这场戏，我有两点要指出。

1149
00:49:19.140 --> 00:49:19.740
What are they?
哪两点？

