我听到背景里有公鸡打鸣吗？

1385
00:57:56.300 --> 00:57:57.120
Yes, guys.
是的，伙计们。

1386
00:57:57.400 --> 00:57:58.080
Yes, you do.
你们确实听到了。

1387
00:57:58.900 --> 00:58:01.120
It's at 13 minutes, 34 seconds.
就在13分34秒的时候。

1388
00:58:01.760 --> 00:58:06.820
There was a house in our vicinity, and they had some chickens and a rooster.
我们附近有一户人家，他们养了一些鸡和一只公鸡。

1389
00:58:07.060 --> 00:58:07.980
And it was a challenge.
那真是一个挑战。

1390
00:58:08.120 --> 00:58:08.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1391
00:58:08.740 --> 00:58:12.340
Because you can't make a rooster not crow when it wants to crow.
因为你没法阻止公鸡在想打鸣的时候不打鸣。

1392
00:58:12.680 --> 00:58:16.480
Also, Jenna, do you remember the year that there was like a flock of parrots?
还有，珍娜，你还记得那一年有一群鹦鹉吗？

1393
00:58:17.080 --> 00:58:17.480
Yes.
记得。

1394
00:58:17.780 --> 00:58:19.540
That like were living in that tree.
它们就住在树上。

1395
00:58:19.760 --> 00:58:21.920
And parrots are so loud, you guys.
伙计们，鹦鹉真的太吵了。

1396
00:58:22.040 --> 00:58:23.240
They're like, wah, wah, wah.
它们叫起来就像，哇，哇，哇。

1397
00:58:23.820 --> 00:58:25.240
So I was like-
所以我当时就想——

1398
00:58:25.240 --> 00:58:28.840
And when they're in a group, they get a bolster of confidence.
而且当它们聚在一起时，胆子就壮了。

1399
00:58:29.140 --> 00:58:29.840
They really do.
确实如此。

1400
00:58:29.960 --> 00:58:31.020
They're super chatty.
它们超级爱叫。

1401
00:58:31.500 --> 00:58:35.740
I remember this because I was like, Kenneth Paul, who did my makeup, I was like, there
我记得这件事，因为当时我对负责给我化妆的肯尼斯·保罗说，你看那里

1402
00:58:35.740 --> 00:58:36.960
is a flock of parrots.
有一群鹦鹉。

1403
00:58:37.100 --> 00:58:40.980
And he said, Angela Faith, because he always called you by your first and middle name.
他说，安吉拉·费斯，因为他总是连名带姓地叫你。

1404
00:58:41.240 --> 00:58:44.520
He said, Angela Faith, don't you mean a pandemonium of parrots?
他说，安吉拉·费斯，你难道不是想说一群鹦鹉吗？

1405
00:58:44.520 --> 00:58:46.860
Is that what a group of parrots is called?
鹦鹉群是这么叫的吗？

1406
00:58:47.080 --> 00:58:47.900
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1407
00:58:48.320 --> 00:58:48.680
Oh.
哦。

1408
00:58:49.260 --> 00:58:51.680
We also had a fan question from Charlotte M.
我们还收到一个来自夏洛特·M的粉丝提问。

1409
00:58:51.820 --> 00:58:54.620
She's wondering, where the heck is Rainn
她想知道，雷恩·威尔逊的麦克风发射器到底

1410
00:58:54.620 --> 00:58:56.500
Wilson's mic pack, right?
在哪儿，对吧？

1411
00:58:56.680 --> 00:58:57.120
Yeah.
没错。

1412
00:58:57.120 --> 00:58:59.340
I'll tell you what, there was no mic pack.
我告诉你吧，根本没有麦克风发射器。

1413
00:58:59.600 --> 00:59:02.620
They had to capture all of his sound on a boom microphone only.
他们只能完全靠吊杆麦克风来收录他的声音。

1414
00:59:02.840 --> 00:59:02.980
Yeah.
是啊。

1415
00:59:03.140 --> 00:59:04.540
They couldn't fit it under his paws.
他们没法把它塞进他的爪子里。

1416
00:59:04.860 --> 00:59:05.180
So.
所以。

1417
00:59:06.820 --> 00:59:08.400
What has happened to you?
你怎么了？

1418
00:59:08.520 --> 00:59:09.300
That's champagne.
那是香槟。

1419
00:59:09.500 --> 00:59:10.740
That's the champagne talking.
那是香槟在作祟。

1420
00:59:11.240 --> 00:59:12.840
That crept up on us.
我们不知不觉就喝多了。

1421
00:59:12.960 --> 00:59:13.340
It did.
确实。

1422
00:59:13.600 --> 00:59:14.040
Slowly.
慢慢地。

1423
00:59:14.480 --> 00:59:15.640
Champagne sneaks up on you.
香槟总是让人防不胜防。

1424
00:59:15.920 --> 00:59:17.140
That's the problem with champagne.
这就是香槟的问题所在。

1425
00:59:17.900 --> 00:59:19.020
Champagne makes me fun.
香槟让我变得很有趣。

1426
00:59:19.420 --> 00:59:20.180
It does?
是吗？

1427
00:59:20.400 --> 00:59:20.540
Yeah.
对。

1428
00:59:21.120 --> 00:59:23.220
What can I expect from this afternoon?
今天下午我还能期待什么呢？

1429
00:59:23.520 --> 00:59:24.500
I don't know.
我不知道。

1430
00:59:25.100 --> 00:59:28.780
I had to stop drinking it because I have to drive home.
我得停止喝它了，因为我还要开车回家。

1431
