你不记得？

1632
01:07:29.420 --> 01:07:33.620
Oh, see, this is the thing I used to love to do where I read every detail of a call
噢，你看，我以前最喜欢做的事就是阅读通告单上的每一个细节。

1633
01:07:33.620 --> 01:07:33.960
sheet.
没错，你确实会看。

1634
01:07:34.140 --> 01:07:34.640
Yes, you would.
我会到现场然后问，为什么《好莱坞娱乐新闻》的人会在这儿？

1635
01:07:35.080 --> 01:07:37.760
I would show up and be like, why is Access Hollywood here?
然后你就会说，安吉拉，通告单上写着呢。

1636
01:07:37.920 --> 01:07:39.840
And you'd be like, Angela, it's on the call sheet.
而且他们可能上周就在你的拖车里放了备忘录。

1637
01:07:40.160 --> 01:07:43.260
And they put a memo in your trailer probably last week.
我直接从那张纸上跨过去了。

1638
01:07:43.380 --> 01:07:44.120
I stepped right over that piece of paper.
她真的会那样。

1639
01:07:44.120 --> 01:07:44.820
She really would.
她的地板上会堆满备忘录。

1640
01:07:44.920 --> 01:07:46.860
There'd be a pile of memos on her floor.
我会把那些纸踢到一边。

1641
01:07:47.060 --> 01:07:47.800
I'd kick the papers to the side.
好吧。

1642
01:07:48.000 --> 01:07:48.340
All right.
所以当你在外景地拍摄时，你会停好车，他们会在一个大停车场里放置发型和化妆拖车，

1643
01:07:48.460 --> 01:07:53.060
So when you shoot on Location, you park your car and they have the hair and makeup trailers
他们称之为大本营。

1644
01:07:53.060 --> 01:07:55.500
in a big parking lot and they call it Base Camp.
那是餐饮服务商搭建食品帐篷的地方。

1645
01:07:56.000 --> 01:07:58.680
This is where the caterers will set up their food tent.
也是你吃午饭的地方。

1646
01:07:58.680 --> 01:07:59.840
It's where you eat lunch.
但很多时候，大本营离实际拍摄地点非常远。

1647
01:08:00.280 --> 01:08:04.800
But a lot of times Base Camp is really far away from the actual shooting location.
这次的情况就是这样。

1648
01:08:04.800 --> 01:08:06.420
And that was the case here.
从大本营到尼古拉餐厅坐面包车大约需要15分钟。

1649
01:08:06.620 --> 01:08:12.200
It was about a 15-minute van ride to get from Base Camp to Nicola's Restaurant.
所以他们必须安排一个面包车时刻表，把所有人都接送到片场。

1650
01:08:12.200 --> 01:08:17.260
So they had to have a van schedule to shuttle all of these people to set.
所以他们必须安排一个面包车时刻表，把所有人都接送到片场。

1651
01:08:17.460 --> 01:08:18.680
And here's what it said.
上面是这么写的。

1652
01:08:18.960 --> 01:08:26.240
It said breakfast would be available as of 5.15 and then you could take one of six vans to set.
上面写着早餐从5点15分开始供应，然后你可以乘坐六辆面包车中的一辆去片场。

1653
01:08:26.240 --> 01:08:33.080
They left at 5.42 a.m., 6.00 a.m., 6.12 a.m.
它们出发的时间分别是早上5点42分、6点整、6点12分。

1654
01:08:33.220 --> 01:08:38.220
And they designated this van for our grip and electric crew, 6.30 a.m.
他们把早上6点30分那辆车指定给了我们的灯光和电力组。

1655
01:08:38.700 --> 01:08:42.800
And then there was one last van at 6.42 a.m.
然后最后一辆车是在6点42分出发。

1656
01:08:42.940 --> 01:08:45.860
And in all caps, it said, this is the late van.
上面用全大写字母写着：这是最后一班车。

1657
01:08:46.520 --> 01:08:48.300
You did not want to be on the late van.
你绝对不想坐那班车。

1658
01:08:48.440 --> 01:08:48.600
Don't do it.
千万别坐。

1659
01:08:49.100 --> 01:08:49.720
No, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不。

1660
01:08:50.060 --> 01:08:56.680
There were also additional shuttles for the cast and the background actors that were set to leave at 7 a.m.
另外还有为演员和背景演员准备的班车，定于早上7点出发。

1661
01:08:57.080 --> 01:09:01.560
So the idea was the crew would get there, set up all the lights, and then the actors would land.
所以计划是工作人员先到，把灯光都架好，然后演员再到。

1662
01:09:01.820 --> 01:09:03.900
The hair and makeup folks would ride with the actors.
发型和化妆师会和演员同车。

1663
01:09:04.280 --> 01:09:05.360
That's the van schedule.
这就是面包车的时间表。

1664
01:09:05.360 --> 01:09:08.160
That was Randy's job to make that van schedule.
制定这个时间表是兰迪的工作。

1665
01:09:08.440 --> 01:09:09.500
He did a fantastic job.
他做得非常出色。

1666
01:09:09.940 --> 01:09:12.000
So Dwight never makes it to the restaurant.
所以德怀特一直没能赶到餐厅。

1667
01:09:12.000 --> 01:09:13.680
He calls and says he hit a bear.
他打电话来说他撞到了一只熊。

1668
01:09:14.260 --> 01:09:16.940
And Michael just believes it.
而迈克尔居然就信了。

1669
01:09:17.100 --> 01:09:18.100
Not just Michael.
不只是迈克尔。

1670
01:09:18.440 --> 01:09:21.520
I will have you know that Pam and Ryan don't even raise an eyebrow.
我得告诉你，帕姆和瑞安连眼皮都没抬一下。

1671
01:09:21.720 --> 01:09:26.840
They don't even look up from their menu when Michael says Dwight hit a bear, but he's on the way.
当迈克尔说德怀特撞了熊但正在赶来的路上时，他们甚至连菜单都没抬头看一眼。

1672
01:09:27.240 --> 01:09:28.980
How many bears has Dwight hit?
德怀特到底撞过多少只熊？

1673
01:09:29.200 --> 01:09:30.920
Why is this so believable?
为什么这事儿这么可信？

1674
01:09:31.420 --> 01:09:33.560
They get back to Michael Scott Paper Company.
他们回到迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1675
01:09:33.560 --> 01:09:35.500
They discover they've been robbed.
发现被抢劫了。

1676
01:09:35.900 --> 01:09:36.620
Dwight calls.
德怀特打来电话。

1677
01:09:36.800 --> 01:09:38.940
Michael is like, I don't have time to talk.
迈克尔说，我没时间跟你聊。

1678
01:09:39.080 --> 01:09:40.080
We've been robbed.
我们被抢了。

1679
01:09:40.900 --> 01:09:44.400
And once again, Pam and Ryan are like, it was Dwight.
而帕姆和瑞安又一次觉得，肯定是德怀特干的。

1680
01:09:44.720 --> 01:09:45.100
Yeah.
没错。

1681
01:09:45.420 --> 01:09:49.220
This is when Dwight is going to start poaching the clients off the Rolodex.
这就是德怀特开始从通讯录里挖客户的时候。

1682
01:09:49.380 --> 01:09:55.620
And to get back at him, Michael is going to eat his meatball parm that he brought back for him, which is so funny.
为了报复他，迈克尔要吃掉德怀特给他带回来的肉丸帕尔马干酪，这太搞笑了。

1683
01:09:55.620 --> 01:09:57.980
He goes, Dwight says, I knew you were going to do that.
他说，德怀特说，我就知道你会这么做。

1684
01:09:58.120 --> 01:10:01.740
And that's why I made you order it because it's the worst thing on their menu.
所以我才让你点这个，因为这是他们菜单上最难吃的东西。

1685
01:10:02.120 --> 01:10:05.140
And then the way Steve is so disgusted by it.
还有史蒂夫表现出的那种厌恶感。

1686
01:10:05.300 --> 01:10:09.200
Why is it so funny to watch Steve eat food that he's disgusted with?
为什么看史蒂夫吃他觉得恶心的食物会这么好笑？

1687
01:10:09.340 --> 01:10:09.480
Anything with food.
任何跟食物有关的都行。

1688
01:10:09.800 --> 01:10:10.400
It's hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1689
01:10:10.740 --> 01:10:13.120
Well, in Casual Friday, he's going to eat everybody's lunch.
嗯，在《休闲星期五》那集里，他要把所有人的午餐都吃掉。

1690
01:10:13.120 --> 01:10:14.040
And it's very, very funny.
那真的非常、非常搞笑。

1691
01:10:14.140 --> 01:10:15.000
I can't wait to get to that.
我迫不及待想讲到那儿了。

1692
01:10:15.100 --> 01:10:16.540
There's some good bloopers from that, too.
那集里还有一些很棒的NG镜头。

1693
01:10:17.020 --> 01:10:18.680
Listen, there was a deleted scene.
听着，有个被删减的片段。

1694
01:10:18.880 --> 01:10:23.360
As Dwight is poaching everyone's clients, he really crosses the line with Ryan.
当德怀特挖走所有人的客户时，他真的惹恼了瑞安。

1695
01:10:24.700 --> 01:10:29.680
Because Ryan's uncle chooses Dwight over the Michael Scott Paper Company.
因为瑞安的叔叔选择了德怀特，而不是迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1696
01:10:29.920 --> 01:10:30.120
What?
什么？

1697
01:10:30.420 --> 01:10:30.580
Yeah.
是的。

1698
01:10:30.720 --> 01:10:32.280
And there's some really good Pam sass.
而且帕姆有一些非常犀利的吐槽。

1699
01:10:32.400 --> 01:10:33.120
We got to hear it.
我们得听听。

1700
01:10:33.980 --> 01:10:35.780
Dwight just got Howard family dry cleaners.
德怀特刚拿下了霍华德家族的干洗店。

1701
01:10:36.840 --> 01:10:37.600
Uncle Dave?
戴夫叔叔？

1702
01:10:37.720 --> 01:10:39.480
Little jerk is undercutting us big time.
那小混蛋在大幅压低我们的价格。

1703
01:10:39.700 --> 01:10:43.540
He is actually taking a loss and paying the difference out of pocket.
他甚至在亏本经营，自掏腰包补差价。

1704
01:10:43.680 --> 01:10:44.420
That's my family.
这就是我的家人。

1705
01:10:45.400 --> 01:10:48.880
When you mess with my family, I can't be responsible for my actions.
当你招惹我的家人时，我可没法保证自己会做出什么事来。

1706
01:10:49.540 --> 01:10:51.600
When are you ever responsible for your actions?
你什么时候能保证过自己的行为？

1707
01:10:51.720 --> 01:10:52.760
Get off my ass, you hag.
别烦我了，你这老巫婆。

1708
01:10:52.760 --> 01:10:53.580
Hey, hey, hey.
嘿，嘿，嘿。

1709
01:10:53.740 --> 01:10:55.080
Something about that seems inappropriate.
这话听着不太合适。

1710
01:10:56.600 --> 01:10:58.880
Something about that seems inappropriate.
这话听着不太合适。

1711
01:10:58.980 --> 01:11:00.580
He can't put his finger on it.
他就是说不出哪里不对劲。

1712
01:11:00.800 --> 01:11:04.140
I love the Ryan-Pam rivalry.
我喜欢瑞安和帕姆之间的竞争。

1713
01:11:04.420 --> 01:11:06.020
I just live for it.
我简直太爱看这个了。

1714
01:11:06.520 --> 01:11:07.700
I love it, too.
我也很喜欢。

1715
01:11:08.120 --> 01:11:12.200
I mean, I just loved working with these guys for this period of time.
我是说，我真的很喜欢这段时间与这些人共事。

1716
01:11:12.300 --> 01:11:13.540
I bet it was so much fun.
我敢说那一定很有趣。

1717
01:11:13.540 --> 01:11:23.740
Well, now we're going to get into a pretty fun bit where Michael is going to walk in to HarperCollins with Dwight on the phone.
好了，现在我们要进入一个非常有趣的片段，迈克尔要带着电话里的德怀特走进哈珀柯林斯出版社。

1718
01:11:23.900 --> 01:11:27.020
He's like, I'm going to let you listen to me still, your biggest client.
他说，我要让你继续听着，你最大的客户。

1719
01:11:27.440 --> 01:11:30.440
And Dwight's like, no, and takes off.
德怀特说，不，然后就走了。

1720
01:11:30.440 --> 01:11:33.280
And he gets in the car all the while listening.
他一边听着一边上了车。

1721
01:11:33.700 --> 01:11:35.320
That was so funny.
那太搞笑了。

1722
01:11:35.460 --> 01:11:38.540
Rain in the car when he was like, paper is the manure.
雷恩在车里说那句“纸就是肥料”的时候。

1723
01:11:39.280 --> 01:11:40.300
And on time.
而且还很准时。

1724
01:11:42.150 --> 01:11:43.730
I wrote down that quote, too.
我也记下了那句台词。

1725
01:11:44.190 --> 01:11:45.470
Do I need that on a mug?
我需要把它印在杯子上吗？

1726
01:11:45.630 --> 01:11:46.990
We might need it on a mug.
我们可能确实需要把它印在杯子上。

1727
01:11:47.150 --> 01:11:48.370
Paper is the manure.
纸就是肥料。

1728
01:11:50.190 --> 01:11:52.470
We had a fan question from Sydney S.
我们收到一个来自悉尼·S的粉丝提问。

1729
01:11:52.610 --> 01:11:57.190
who said, how did you guys film that scene of Dwight driving to Mr. Schofield's office?
她问，你们是怎么拍摄德怀特开车去斯科菲尔德先生办公室那场戏的？

1730
01:11:57.450 --> 01:11:59.570
Was Steve really on the other end of the phone?
史蒂夫真的在电话那头吗？

1731
01:12:00.470 --> 01:12:02.970
No, Steve was not on the other end of the phone.
不，史蒂夫当时并不在电话那头。

1732
01:12:03.710 --> 01:12:05.850
And I talked with Randy about this.
我和兰迪聊过这件事。

1733
01:12:06.450 --> 01:12:07.770
Rain is really driving.
雷恩是真的在开车。

1734
01:12:08.030 --> 01:12:08.890
He's free driving.
他是自由驾驶。

1735
01:12:09.130 --> 01:12:10.770
He is not hooked up to anything.
他没有连接任何设备。

1736
01:12:10.970 --> 01:12:13.750
It looked like it to me, just the way he pulled into the parking lot.
我看的时候觉得是，尤其是他开进停车场的那种方式。

1737
01:12:13.970 --> 01:12:15.330
Yeah, the whole time.
是的，全程都是。

1738
01:12:15.330 --> 01:12:18.710
So they had LAPD officers on motorcycles.
所以他们安排了洛杉矶警局的摩托车警察。

1739
01:12:19.150 --> 01:12:22.490
So no one would sort of interfere with the shot or rain driving.
这样就不会有人干扰拍摄或者雷恩的驾驶。

1740
01:12:22.790 --> 01:12:23.470
Yes, correct.
是的，没错。

1741
01:12:23.850 --> 01:12:26.790
And there's also a crew van following behind.
而且后面还有一辆剧组的面包车跟着。

1742
01:12:27.210 --> 01:12:28.970
But here's how they got that shot.
但他们是这样拍到那个镜头的。

1743
01:12:29.430 --> 01:12:31.990
Matt Soane, our camera operator, was in the front seat.
我们的摄影师马特·索恩坐在前排。

1744
01:12:32.370 --> 01:12:32.890
Oh.
哦。

1745
01:12:33.010 --> 01:12:33.670
Filming rain.
拍摄雷恩。

1746
01:12:34.090 --> 01:12:37.530
Our sound engineer, Ben Patrick, was in the back seat recording sound.
我们的录音师本·帕特里克坐在后座录音。

1747
01:12:37.710 --> 01:12:40.690
And our director, Paul Feig, was also in the back seat.
我们的导演保罗·费格也坐在后座。

1748
01:12:40.990 --> 01:12:43.190
That was not a big back seat.
那后座可不宽敞。

1749
01:12:43.310 --> 01:12:44.610
I have been in that car.
我坐过那辆车。

1750
01:12:44.610 --> 01:12:45.990
That is tiny.
空间太小了。

1751
01:12:46.290 --> 01:12:46.850
I know.
我知道。

1752
01:12:47.270 --> 01:12:50.790
And Randy said, we did not have a two-way phone setup.
兰迪说，我们当时没有双向通话的设备。

1753
01:12:51.050 --> 01:12:52.630
It was just too unreliable.
那太不可靠了。

1754
01:12:52.910 --> 01:12:59.370
And so Randy's guess is that Paul Feig was reading Steve's dialogue so that Rain could react to it.
所以兰迪猜测是保罗·费格在读史蒂夫的台词，好让雷恩能做出反应。

1755
01:12:59.450 --> 01:12:59.630
Yeah.
没错。

1756
01:13:00.110 --> 01:13:00.550
Amazing.
太棒了。

1757
01:13:00.970 --> 01:13:03.070
I wish we had a picture of those four guys in the car.
真希望我们有那四个人在车里的照片。

1758
01:13:03.370 --> 01:13:07.130
Can we talk about what happens when Dwight arrives at Mr. Schofield's office?
我们能聊聊德怀特到达斯科菲尔德先生办公室时发生了什么吗？

1759
01:13:07.390 --> 01:13:07.830
Finally.
终于来了。

1760
01:13:07.830 --> 01:13:09.250
I lived for this.
我一直盼着这一幕。

1761
01:13:09.450 --> 01:13:12.850
I had to know if this was scripted or improvised.
我必须知道这是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的。

1762
01:13:13.010 --> 01:13:15.050
So Dwight is going to run in.
德怀特跑了进去。

1763
01:13:15.170 --> 01:13:17.370
First of all, he's changing into his mustard shirt.
首先，他换上了那件芥末色的衬衫。

1764
01:13:17.490 --> 01:13:18.330
I loved that detail.
我喜欢这个细节。

1765
01:13:18.550 --> 01:13:19.210
I loved that detail.
我喜欢这个细节。

1766
01:13:19.430 --> 01:13:23.450
And then when he gets to the receptionist, he does this crazy spin move.
然后当他走到前台时，他做了一个疯狂的旋转动作。

1767
01:13:23.450 --> 01:13:26.110
And then Dwight says spin move.
接着德怀特说了句“旋转动作”。

1768
01:13:26.350 --> 01:13:28.610
And I was like, did Rain improvise that?
我当时就在想，这是雷恩即兴发挥的吗？

1769
01:13:28.750 --> 01:13:29.330
I've got to know.
我一定要搞清楚。

1770
01:13:29.670 --> 01:13:31.250
Jenna, it was 100% in the script.
珍娜，这百分之百是剧本里写的。

1771
01:13:31.870 --> 01:13:32.310
Everything.
全都是。

1772
01:13:32.690 --> 01:13:33.790
Even the spin move.
连那个旋转动作也是。

1773
01:13:33.970 --> 01:13:34.450
All of it.
全都是。

1774
01:13:34.450 --> 01:13:40.650
I found an old interview with Rain where he said that one time he did a somersault.
我翻到了一篇雷恩的旧采访，他说有一次他做了一个空翻。

1775
01:13:41.590 --> 01:13:44.950
And he said he thought that it would look extra stealthy.
他说他觉得那样看起来会格外隐秘。

1776
01:13:45.150 --> 01:13:45.330
Yeah.
是啊。

1777
01:13:45.470 --> 01:13:50.470
When they watched it back, it looked, quote, like a manatee doing ballet at SeaWorld.
当他们回看录像时，他说看起来“就像一只在海洋世界跳芭蕾的海牛”。

1778
01:13:51.890 --> 01:13:54.410
He also said they did about five takes.
他还说他们大约拍了五次。

1779
01:13:54.850 --> 01:13:59.330
I also have a little guest star breakdown for Mr. Schofield's receptioniSt.
我还整理了一份斯科菲尔德先生前台接待员的客串演员资料。

1780
01:13:59.330 --> 01:14:07.230
She was played by Angela Campola-Sanders, who was our casting associate on The Office since season four.
她由安吉拉·坎波拉-桑德斯饰演，她从第四季开始就是我们《办公室》的选角助理。

1781
01:14:07.450 --> 01:14:09.070
This is her only acting credit.
这是她唯一的演艺作品。

1782
01:14:09.290 --> 01:14:09.610
That's awesome.
太厉害了。

1783
01:14:09.610 --> 01:14:12.630
But she played Mr. Schofield's receptioniSt.
但她确实演了斯科菲尔德先生的前台。

1784
01:14:12.870 --> 01:14:16.810
Pretty much everyone in our casting office made it into the episode at some point.
我们选角办公室的每个人几乎都在剧集的某个时刻露过脸。

1785
01:14:16.910 --> 01:14:17.490
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

1786
01:14:17.650 --> 01:14:18.110
I do too.
我也是。

1787
01:14:18.790 --> 01:14:26.010
Dwight is about to dig himself into a big old hole because he doesn't understand Michael's Rolodex or Michael's color coding info.
德怀特正准备自掘坟墓，因为他不了解迈克尔的电话簿或他的颜色编码信息。

1788
01:14:26.010 --> 01:14:29.770
Michael has a talking head where he says, I color code all my info.
迈克尔有个单人访谈，他说：“我用颜色给所有信息做了编码。”

1789
01:14:29.950 --> 01:14:31.170
I wrote gay son in green.
“我用绿色标记了‘同性恋儿子’。”

1790
01:14:31.370 --> 01:14:32.110
Green means go.
“绿色代表通行。”

1791
01:14:32.310 --> 01:14:34.350
So I know to go ahead and shut up about it.
“所以我知道该继续说下去还是闭嘴。”

1792
01:14:34.850 --> 01:14:35.130
Yes.
没错。

1793
01:14:35.210 --> 01:14:37.510
And orange means orange you glad you didn't bring it up.
“橙色代表‘很高兴你没提这事’（Orange you glad）。”

1794
01:14:37.750 --> 01:14:39.390
Most colors mean don't say it.
“大多数颜色都意味着别提它。”

1795
01:14:39.830 --> 01:14:40.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1796
01:14:40.430 --> 01:14:41.570
But Dwight doesn't know that.
但德怀特不知道这些。

1797
01:14:42.230 --> 01:14:42.530
Yeah.
没错。

1798
01:14:42.690 --> 01:14:47.410
So Dwight is basically saying all the things that are color coded to not be said.
所以德怀特基本上把所有被颜色编码标记为“不能说”的事情全说了出来。

1799
01:14:47.610 --> 01:14:47.810
Right.
对。

1800
01:14:47.810 --> 01:14:57.570
Well, before we wrap up this heavy competition between Mike, wait, this episode, that's the champagne.
好吧，在我们结束迈克尔和……等等，这集里，那是香槟的声音。

1801
01:14:57.750 --> 01:14:58.070
I know.
我知道。

1802
01:14:58.170 --> 01:15:01.290
And the champagne, you have a nickname for everyone in your champagne brain.
还有香槟，你那香槟脑袋里给每个人都起了绰号。

1803
01:15:01.390 --> 01:15:01.850
Mike.
迈克。

1804
01:15:02.030 --> 01:15:02.410
Mike.
迈克。

1805
01:15:02.790 --> 01:15:03.170
Dwighty.
德怀特。

1806
01:15:05.590 --> 01:15:06.270
Okay.
好吧。

1807
01:15:07.410 --> 01:15:13.170
I think we should go back and wrap up this Andy Jim storyline.
我觉得我们应该回去把安迪和吉姆的故事线收个尾。

1808
01:15:13.590 --> 01:15:13.810
Okay.
好的。

1809
01:15:14.010 --> 01:15:16.330
We both had to stop drinking champagne, by the way.
顺便说一下，我们俩都得戒掉香槟了。

1810
01:15:16.850 --> 01:15:17.650
We did.
确实。

1811
01:15:18.030 --> 01:15:20.350
It just, it's so interesting.
这真的，太有意思了。

1812
01:15:20.530 --> 01:15:22.490
Scotch and Splenda was like, woo-boo, woo-boo.
苏格兰威士忌加代糖就像是，呜呼，呜呼。

1813
01:15:22.650 --> 01:15:25.050
But champagne were like, I can't talk right now.
但香槟就像是，我现在没法说话。

1814
01:15:25.290 --> 01:15:25.690
Yeah.
是啊。

1815
01:15:25.810 --> 01:15:28.250
I still really do love the Scotch and Splenda.
我依然真的很喜欢苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

1816
01:15:28.470 --> 01:15:28.890
Me too.
我也是。

1817
01:15:28.890 --> 01:15:29.930
I have to say.
我不得不说。

1818
01:15:29.930 --> 01:15:31.110
It's a really good drink.
这真的是款好酒。

1819
01:15:31.110 --> 01:15:35.670
And we got some letters from people who said it's basically an old fashioned if we'd added
我们收到了一些人的来信，说如果我们再加点

1820
01:15:35.670 --> 01:15:36.530
a few orange bitters.
橙味苦精，它基本上就是一杯古典鸡尾酒了。

1821
01:15:36.670 --> 01:15:38.150
And that's what it tasted like to me.
我喝着也是那个味儿。

1822
01:15:38.250 --> 01:15:38.510
That's right.
没错。

1823
01:15:38.810 --> 01:15:40.770
Because I guess you would add like a sugar.
因为我想你大概会加点糖之类的。

1824
01:15:41.050 --> 01:15:41.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1825
01:15:41.770 --> 01:15:45.350
A muddled kind of sugary syrup to the Scotch.
往苏格兰威士忌里加点捣碎的糖浆。

1826
01:15:45.350 --> 01:15:45.530
Right.
对。

1827
01:15:45.530 --> 01:15:47.550
And so that's what the Splenda is doing.
所以代糖起的就是这个作用。

1828
01:15:48.030 --> 01:15:48.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1829
01:15:48.610 --> 01:15:50.650
But champagne just makes us go, what?
但香槟只会让我们觉得，什么？

1830
01:15:50.750 --> 01:15:51.550
What are we talking about?
我们在聊什么？

1831
01:15:51.690 --> 01:15:52.030
What's happening?
发生什么了？

1832
01:15:52.030 --> 01:15:52.410
I know.
我知道。

1833
01:15:52.670 --> 01:15:52.850
Okay.
好吧。

1834
01:15:53.330 --> 01:15:53.930
All right.
行吧。

1835
01:15:54.970 --> 01:15:55.390
See?
你看？

1836
01:15:55.650 --> 01:15:56.170
I know.
我知道。

1837
01:15:56.290 --> 01:15:57.430
I'm like, what am I talking about?
我都在想，我在说什么呢？

1838
01:15:57.610 --> 01:15:57.790
Okay.
好吧。

1839
01:15:57.990 --> 01:15:59.130
So Andy and Jim.
那么安迪和吉姆。

1840
01:16:00.290 --> 01:16:03.550
Andy is going to tell the whole bullpen that Jim is upset.
安迪打算告诉整个办公区的人说吉姆很心烦。

1841
01:16:04.830 --> 01:16:09.810
And Phyllis is going to be like, Andy, I think Jim is just messing with you.
然后菲利斯会说，安迪，我觉得吉姆只是在逗你玩。

1842
01:16:10.050 --> 01:16:14.430
And then there's that smug shot of Jim in the kitchen looking out through the blinds
接着就是那个吉姆在厨房里透过百叶窗往外看的自鸣得意的镜头，

1843
01:16:14.430 --> 01:16:16.090
with that grin on his face.
脸上带着那种坏笑。

1844
01:16:16.090 --> 01:16:21.250
We had a fan question from Raya H and Poonet B.
我们收到了来自Raya H和Poonet B的粉丝提问。

1845
01:16:21.690 --> 01:16:25.170
Can we talk about how douchey Jim is being in this episode?
我们能聊聊吉姆在这一集里有多混蛋吗？

1846
01:16:25.710 --> 01:16:28.790
Andy was being really supportive and genuinely cared for Jim.
安迪当时真的很支持吉姆，也是真心关心他。

1847
01:16:28.950 --> 01:16:35.150
And while Andy's concern might have been misguided or nosy, I think it came from a good place.
虽然安迪的关心可能有点找错方向或者多管闲事，但我认为他是出于好意。

1848
01:16:35.390 --> 01:16:41.810
We'd really like to get your take on this prank that Jim pulls on Andy because we think
我们真的很想听听你们对吉姆捉弄安迪这件事的看法，因为我们觉得

1849
01:16:41.810 --> 01:16:43.890
the prank might have been a little mean-spirited.
这个恶作剧可能有点恶意了。

1850
01:16:44.610 --> 01:16:45.830
I didn't care for it.
我不太喜欢这个恶作剧。

1851
01:16:46.070 --> 01:16:46.810
I didn't either.
我也没有。

1852
01:16:46.950 --> 01:16:48.930
I do think this is a mean-spirited joke.
我确实觉得这是一个恶意的玩笑。

1853
01:16:49.130 --> 01:16:54.370
I mean, we already know I don't like pranks and I don't love especially pranks that-
我的意思是，我们都知道我不喜欢恶作剧，尤其是那种……

1854
01:16:54.370 --> 01:16:55.310
At someone's expense.
以他人为代价的恶作剧。

1855
01:16:55.410 --> 01:16:56.770
That play with their emotions.
那种玩弄他人感情的恶作剧。

1856
01:16:57.030 --> 01:16:57.130
Right.
没错。

1857
01:16:57.350 --> 01:17:04.050
I think it was too big of a reaction to Andy's kind of nosy meddling.
我觉得对于安迪那种爱管闲事的行为，这个反应有点太过了。

1858
01:17:04.290 --> 01:17:07.490
And he does have this nice speech, Jim, at the end to Andy.
而且吉姆最后对安迪说了一段很感人的话。

1859
01:17:07.490 --> 01:17:11.950
He's like, listen, I know Angela broke your heart, but you're going to find someone else.
他说，听着，我知道安吉拉伤了你的心，但你会找到别人的。

1860
01:17:12.090 --> 01:17:12.850
You really will.
你真的会找到的。

1861
01:17:13.290 --> 01:17:16.910
So I feel like that was the moment where the writers were like, you know, Jim's not a bad
所以我感觉那一刻编剧们是在表达，你知道，吉姆并不是个坏

1862
01:17:16.910 --> 01:17:17.270
guy.
人。

1863
01:17:17.490 --> 01:17:21.330
Maybe he was trying to show Andy something, but I just didn't like the prank.
也许他只是想教安迪点什么，但我就是不喜欢这个恶作剧。

1864
01:17:21.730 --> 01:17:22.390
Me either.
我也不喜欢。

1865
01:17:22.690 --> 01:17:22.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1866
01:17:23.230 --> 01:17:24.830
Well, I'm glad we discussed that.
好吧，很高兴我们讨论了这个。

1867
01:17:24.970 --> 01:17:25.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1868
01:17:25.130 --> 01:17:25.750
We're with you.
我们支持你。

1869
01:17:25.890 --> 01:17:29.310
So this episode ends with more cheeseball fun.
这一集的结尾是更多关于芝士球的乐趣。

1870
01:17:29.910 --> 01:17:33.710
Michael, Ryan, and Pam, they're trying to see how many cheese puffs can they fit in
迈克尔、瑞安和帕姆，他们试图看看能往嘴里塞多少个

1871
01:17:33.710 --> 01:17:34.310
their mouth?
芝士球？

1872
01:17:34.530 --> 01:17:34.910
32.
32个。

1873
01:17:35.290 --> 01:17:36.190
That's the record.
那是纪录。

1874
01:17:36.350 --> 01:17:36.510
Yeah.
是啊。

1875
01:17:36.510 --> 01:17:41.230
And then the phone rings and Michael answers it and he's got a mouthful of cheese puffs
然后电话响了，迈克尔接起电话，嘴里塞满了芝士球，

1876
01:17:41.230 --> 01:17:42.070
and we're all laughing.
我们都笑了。

1877
01:17:42.390 --> 01:17:46.310
And while this is happening, you can hear a Michael talking head where he's saying he
就在这期间，你可以听到迈克尔的采访片段，他说他

1878
01:17:46.310 --> 01:17:48.630
wanted to start a company and not a war.
想创办一家公司，而不是发动一场战争。

1879
01:17:49.370 --> 01:17:52.350
Well, this talking head was added later.
嗯，这个采访片段是后来补拍的。

1880
01:17:52.610 --> 01:17:54.230
This was not in the original script.
这不在最初的剧本里。

1881
01:17:54.890 --> 01:18:00.610
Steve shot this a couple weeks after we shot the original episode and all of this footage
史蒂夫是在我们拍完原剧集和所有这些我们吃芝士球的镜头几周后

1882
01:18:00.610 --> 01:18:02.970
of us doing this cheese puffs bit.
补拍的这段。

1883
01:18:03.170 --> 01:18:03.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1884
01:18:03.350 --> 01:18:06.970
This was originally going to be at the end of the cold open.
这原本是打算放在开场戏结尾的。

1885
01:18:07.190 --> 01:18:09.870
So it was all of that was going to live at the top of the episode.
所以所有这些内容原本都是要在剧集开头出现的。

1886
01:18:10.110 --> 01:18:10.510
Yes.
是的。

1887
01:18:10.670 --> 01:18:15.410
But they thought it would be funnier to end the cold open on Pam getting the cheese puffs
但他们觉得以帕姆打着哈欠吃芝士球作为开场戏的结尾会更有趣。

1888
01:18:15.410 --> 01:18:16.510
while she's yawning.
于是他们给这一集加了这个新的结尾片段。

1889
01:18:16.510 --> 01:18:22.470
And then they gave this episode this new tag with the cheese ball bit.
这并不是这一集最初的结尾片段。

1890
01:18:22.470 --> 01:18:25.110
This was not the original tag for the episode.
所以原本并没有开头和结尾的芝士球呼应，而是有一个结尾片段，

1891
01:18:25.350 --> 01:18:30.870
So instead of this bookend of cheese puffs at the beginning and end, there was a tag and
我们确实拍了，我想和大家分享一下。

1892
01:18:30.870 --> 01:18:33.450
we did film it and I want to share it with you guys.
安迪在会议室里，他正在变卖他的婚礼用品。

1893
01:18:33.830 --> 01:18:38.130
So Andy is in the conference room and he is selling off his wedding stuff.
他很坚定。

1894
01:18:38.290 --> 01:18:39.010
He's determined.
依然如此。

1895
01:18:39.370 --> 01:18:39.420
Still.
嗯，你知道，他没能从吉姆和帕姆那里找到买家。

1896
01:18:39.710 --> 01:18:42.410
Well, you know, he didn't get buyers from Jim and Pam.
所以在那个结尾片段里，他把东西卖给其他人，大家都在竞价。

1897
01:18:42.410 --> 01:18:47.410
So in the tag, he's selling it to the rest of the gang and they're all bidding on things.
斯坦利买了米袋，克里德也决定参与进来。

1898
01:18:47.810 --> 01:18:52.010
Stanley buys the rice bags and Creed decides to get in on the action too.
我想我们应该听听那段内容。

1899
01:18:52.370 --> 01:18:53.950
I thought we had to hear a little bit of it.
你为什么在这儿，斯坦利？

1900
01:18:55.070 --> 01:18:56.270
Why are you here, Stanley?
你为什么在这儿，斯坦利？

1901
01:18:56.730 --> 01:18:57.970
I'm here for the rice.
我是来买米的。

1902
01:18:58.310 --> 01:18:58.510
Boom.
砰。

1903
01:18:58.750 --> 01:18:59.090
Sold.
成交。

1904
01:18:59.330 --> 01:19:00.090
100 bags of rice.
100袋大米。

1905
01:19:00.190 --> 01:19:00.630
Stanley Hudson.
斯坦利·哈德森。

1906
01:19:00.870 --> 01:19:04.210
Creed, how would you like a crispy new tuxedo for your funeral?
克里德，你想在葬礼上穿一套崭新的燕尾服吗？

1907
01:19:04.430 --> 01:19:05.690
I'll take the bottom half.
我要下半身那部分。

1908
01:19:07.070 --> 01:19:08.930
I want to go out the same way I came in.
我想怎么来就怎么走。

1909
01:19:09.150 --> 01:19:09.550
Shirtless.
不穿上衣。

1910
01:19:10.970 --> 01:19:15.290
And everyone else starts making bids too, asking questions on things.
然后其他人也开始竞价，问各种问题。

1911
01:19:16.150 --> 01:19:20.710
Angela is not in the scene, but she walks by and had this talking head.
安吉拉没出现在这一幕里，但她走过时录了这段采访。

1912
01:19:20.870 --> 01:19:21.970
It was in the shooting draft.
剧本初稿里有这一段。

1913
01:19:22.410 --> 01:19:24.090
I don't know why I'm down.
我不知道我为什么难过。

1914
01:19:24.350 --> 01:19:29.610
I guess I always thought that Andy would save the stuff from our wedding just in case.
我想我一直以为安迪会把我们婚礼的东西留着，以防万一。

1915
01:19:30.090 --> 01:19:31.890
No, it's stupid.
不，这太蠢了。

1916
01:19:33.050 --> 01:19:37.510
Just in case I married someone else and he decided to throw us a wedding.
以防我嫁给了别人，而他决定为我们举办一场婚礼。

1917
01:19:37.670 --> 01:19:38.750
I told you it was stupid.
我跟你说过这很蠢。

1918
01:19:42.210 --> 01:19:44.710
I guess there were some things in there that Angela liked.
我想里面有些东西是安吉拉喜欢的。

1919
01:19:44.930 --> 01:19:45.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1920
01:19:45.610 --> 01:19:47.370
And maybe she hoped would make a comeback.
也许她希望这些东西能派上用场。

1921
01:19:48.410 --> 01:19:50.630
Ah, so there you have it, guys.
啊，情况就是这样，伙计们。

1922
01:19:50.990 --> 01:19:52.250
100 episodes.
100集了。

1923
01:19:52.750 --> 01:19:53.670
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1924
01:19:53.670 --> 01:19:55.430
We got it in just before the holidays.
我们在假期前刚好完成了。

1925
01:19:55.710 --> 01:19:56.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1926
01:19:56.270 --> 01:19:58.450
I'm glad because that's always like a very crazy time.
我很高兴，因为那段时间总是非常疯狂。

1927
01:19:58.630 --> 01:19:59.290
It is.
确实。

1928
01:19:59.530 --> 01:20:02.250
The Halloween to New Year's.
从万圣节到新年这段时间。

1929
01:20:02.270 --> 01:20:04.390
It's a sprint to the end, I always say.
我常说，这是冲向终点的短跑。

1930
01:20:05.090 --> 01:20:07.730
Well, listen, we're going to have a few breaks coming up.
好了，听着，我们接下来会有几次休息。

1931
01:20:07.830 --> 01:20:09.890
We do take a break at Thanksgiving.
感恩节我们会休息。

1932
01:20:09.890 --> 01:20:11.870
We take a break at Christmas and New Year's.
圣诞节和新年我们也会休息。

1933
01:20:11.970 --> 01:20:17.290
We will have some great reruns of episodes with fun little new stuff at the top.
我们会重播一些精彩的剧集，并在开头加入一些有趣的新内容。

1934
01:20:17.470 --> 01:20:17.590
Yes.
没错。

1935
01:20:17.590 --> 01:20:19.170
So be sure to listen to that stuff.
所以一定要收听那些内容。

1936
